  }
 ],
 "synopsis": "Whirlpool of India shares surged 20% to hit the upper circuit at Rs 865.35 on the BSE following reports that promoter Whirlpool Mauritius is mulling the sale of its entire remaining 39.76% stake in the household appliances maker. The deal is reportedly in its final stages with an announcement expected in coming weeks, and potential buyers include large investors and a major multinational consumer durables company. The promoter has been reducing its holding from 75% down to 39.76% over the past three years, including an 11.24% stake sale last year.",
 "ticker": "WHIRLPOOL.NS",
